c0723
00:40:33.939 --> 00:40:35.340
He didn't want to convert.

c0724
00:40:35.340 --> 00:40:38.419
His father converted.

c0725
00:40:38.419 --> 00:40:43.020
Now, another example, David Ricardo,

c0726
00:40:43.020 --> 00:40:46.659
the greatest, the most important economist in modern time,

c0727
00:40:46.659 --> 00:40:49.580
the founder of the Bank of England.

c0728
00:40:49.580 --> 00:40:51.139
He founded the Bank of England.

c0729
00:40:51.139 --> 00:40:54.419
That's not a joke.

c0730
00:40:54.419 --> 00:40:57.739
David Ricardo married a Christian.

c0731
00:40:57.739 --> 00:41:05.780
Isaac Pinto, who was the founder of the French Bourse,

c0732
00:41:05.780 --> 00:41:09.340
the French stock market.

c0733
00:41:09.340 --> 00:41:11.820
He did not convert and so on, but I

c0734
00:41:11.820 --> 00:41:14.500
don't know what happened to his children or grandchildren.

c0735
00:41:14.500 --> 00:41:15.260
They disappeared.

c0736
00:41:15.260 --> 00:41:17.780
I mean, they totally, totally, all those families disappeared.

c0737
00:41:17.780 --> 00:41:22.620
The Sephardim lost the West.

c0738
00:41:22.620 --> 00:41:25.419
All right, this is very important, you know.

c0739
00:41:25.419 --> 00:41:29.300
There were a few here, there, and so on, you know.

c0740
00:41:29.300 --> 00:41:31.580
We lost the West, you know.

c0741
00:41:31.580 --> 00:41:40.379
And therefore, we remain mostly Ottoman Empire, North Africa,

c0742
00:41:40.379 --> 00:41:45.580
Middle East, you know, like Iraq and those things.

c0743
00:41:45.580 --> 00:41:47.699
Let me, you raised your hand before.

c0744
00:41:47.699 --> 00:41:50.860
You're trying to be, like, after the return of the French.

c0745
00:41:50.860 --> 00:41:52.179
Yes, yes.

c0746
00:41:53.100 --> 00:41:57.260
The Jews, once after the Shabbatai Sevii movement,

c0747
00:41:57.260 --> 00:41:59.820
came two things that devastated the Jews.

c0748
00:41:59.820 --> 00:42:02.979
Either it was the possibility of reform

c0749
00:42:02.979 --> 00:42:05.739
or the possibility of becoming a citizen, yes.

c0750
00:42:05.739 --> 00:42:08.939
Now, when you go, and I don't want to shock any of you

c0751
00:42:08.939 --> 00:42:11.540
in this now, but when you go to pray

c0752
00:42:11.540 --> 00:42:16.260
in some of the synagogues, all synagogues in Europe,

c0753
00:42:16.260 --> 00:42:20.659
which are traditional, they are, like, reformed.

c0754
00:42:20.659 --> 00:42:23.260
But when you go to Rome, to the main synagogue,

c0755
00:42:23.260 --> 00:42:24.939
they play the organ.

c0756
00:42:24.939 --> 00:42:27.219
I don't know how it is in the Paris synagogue today,

c0757
00:42:27.219 --> 00:42:29.020
in the last synagogue.

c0758
00:42:29.020 --> 00:42:33.699
They have the organ, probably they do have the organ.

c0759
00:42:33.699 --> 00:42:35.699
Yes.

c0760
00:42:35.699 --> 00:42:37.899
Now, they have no more?

c0761
00:42:37.899 --> 00:42:39.739
All right, at one time, they used to have the organ.

c0762
00:42:39.739 --> 00:42:42.100
Now, maybe because there's many Moroccans, North Africans,

c0763
00:42:42.100 --> 00:42:43.020
so on, they come there.

c0764
00:42:43.020 --> 00:42:44.540
But at one time, they had the organ.

c0765
00:42:44.540 --> 00:42:47.500
They had organ, they had organ, and so on.

c0766
00:42:47.500 --> 00:42:50.659
And some of them, they're very, very difficult

c0767
00:42:50.659 --> 00:42:54.419
to distinguish between them and reform,

c0768
00:42:54.419 --> 00:43:01.939
because I just wanted to know that we lost the West.

c0769
00:43:01.939 --> 00:43:08.979
All right, now, what to do?

c0770
00:43:08.979 --> 00:43:10.139
What to do?

c0771
00:43:10.139 --> 00:43:14.979
That is the crisis, the paradigm in the 19th century.

c0772
00:43:14.979 --> 00:43:16.419
What I'm going to tell you is one

c0773
00:43:16.419 --> 00:43:21.219
of the most brilliant chapters in our history.

c0774
00:43:21.219 --> 00:43:23.739
Unfortunately, it's unknown.

c0775
00:43:23.739 --> 00:43:27.500
I've written about it enormously for the last 20, 30 years.

c0776
00:43:27.500 --> 00:43:29.379
And although I've written about it,

c0777
00:43:29.379 --> 00:43:32.580
and some Ashkenaz already are acknowledging the points,

c0778
00:43:32.580 --> 00:43:34.340
of course, without mentioning me.

c0779
00:43:34.340 --> 00:43:39.939
But the truth is that we, Sephardim,

c0780
00:43:39.939 --> 00:43:43.500
are not aware of what happened at the beginning

c0781
00:43:43.500 --> 00:43:47.939
of the 19th century.

c0782
00:43:47.939 --> 00:43:53.379
The most important man was Rabbi Yisrael Moshe Hazzan.

c0783
00:43:53.379 --> 00:43:55.540
Tell me a little about Moshe Hazzan.

c0784
00:43:55.540 --> 00:43:58.340
Moshe Hazzan, the Hazzan family, was

c0785
00:43:58.340 --> 00:44:04.100
the most prestigious rabbinic family known in this.

c0786
00:44:04.100 --> 00:44:06.500
Great-grandparents for generations

c0787
00:44:06.500 --> 00:44:09.419
that had been chief rabbis of Israel.

c0788
00:44:09.419 --> 00:44:12.540
Eliyahu Hazzan was the chief Rabbi of Cairo.

c0789
00:44:15.540 --> 00:44:19.340
Yosef Hazzan was the chief Rabbi, first, of Izmir,

c0790
00:44:19.340 --> 00:44:25.659
then of Istanbul, then of Erez Israel, Rishon Lesion.

c0791
00:44:25.659 --> 00:44:29.659
The cousin of Rabbi Yisrael Moshe Hazzan was Rabbi Haim Palache.

c0792
00:44:29.659 --> 00:44:33.580
He was one of the most prestigious rabbis.

c0793
00:44:33.580 --> 00:44:38.179
When he was a young man, Yisrael Moshe Hazzan

c0794
00:44:38.179 --> 00:44:46.620
is sent as a shaliah from Erez Israel to Western Europe

c0795
00:44:46.620 --> 00:44:48.659
to raise money.

c0796
00:44:48.659 --> 00:44:52.620
Now, the institution of the shalihut

c0797
00:44:52.620 --> 00:44:56.739
was one of the oldest and most important institutions

c0798
00:44:56.739 --> 00:44:58.500
in the Sepharadi world.

c0799
00:44:58.500 --> 00:45:01.459
What this institution consisted of?

c0800
00:45:01.459 --> 00:45:06.699
Jews from all over the Sepharadi world, from the Americas,

c0801
00:45:06.699 --> 00:45:11.699
used to come to places like Barbados, Curaçao, Suriname,

c0802
00:45:11.699 --> 00:45:18.379
New York, Philadelphia, to places as far as Goa in India.

c0803
00:45:18.379 --> 00:45:22.179
The shalihim would come and raise money

c0804
00:45:22.179 --> 00:45:28.100
for the four main yeshivot of the Sephardim, which

c0805
00:45:28.100 --> 00:45:34.620
were in Jerusalem, Safed, Hebron.

c0806
00:45:34.620 --> 00:45:40.899
That's right, Hebron, Jerusalem, Safed, and what else?

c0807
00:45:40.899 --> 00:45:42.500
And Tiberia.

c0808
00:45:42.500 --> 00:45:43.000
That's it.

c0809
00:45:43.000 --> 00:45:44.699
That's the four places.

c0810
00:45:44.699 --> 00:45:48.739
Now, Jews from all over the world would contribute.

c0811
00:45:48.739 --> 00:45:52.699
And therefore, these four cities, Tiberia, Hebron,

c0812
00:45:52.699 --> 00:45:59.100
Jerusalem, Safed, were like the universities of the Jews,

c0813
00:45:59.100 --> 00:46:02.459
whom they used to send as a shaliah.

c0814
00:46:02.459 --> 00:46:06.300
The people they sent as a shaliah was the best that we had,

c0815
00:46:06.300 --> 00:46:10.100
people who eventually will become the chief rabbis of Israel.

c0816
00:46:10.100 --> 00:46:15.060
And the shaliah, the shalihut, lasted for years and years.

c0817
00:46:15.060 --> 00:46:20.340
Yisrael Moshe Hazzan, as a young man in his early 20s, 23,

c0818
00:46:20.340 --> 00:46:23.139
he is sent to Europe.

c0819
00:46:23.139 --> 00:46:30.540
And he goes and he visits places like Prague in Czechoslovakia,

c0820
00:46:30.540 --> 00:46:33.459
Rome.

c0821
00:46:33.459 --> 00:46:36.699
He goes to Amsterdam.

c0822
00:46:36.699 --> 00:46:40.500
He goes to England.

c0823
00:46:40.500 --> 00:46:47.820
And for the first time, he sees what is going on in the world.

c0824
00:46:47.820 --> 00:46:52.820
He discovers both the danger of the reform movement.

c0825
00:46:56.419 --> 00:46:59.620
I want to read for you some of the things that he wrote.

c0826
00:47:00.060 --> 00:47:01.699
It's so amazing.

c0827
00:47:01.699 --> 00:47:05.179
It's so amazing that it simply escapes the mind

c0828
00:47:05.179 --> 00:47:14.580
how a person so many years ago would have been able to,

c0829
00:47:14.580 --> 00:47:25.060
you know, he says like this, he says, he says like this.

c0830
00:47:25.060 --> 00:47:33.179
He says, behold, there it lays before us,

c0831
00:47:33.179 --> 00:47:39.699
the great corruption that prevails among us in Europe,

c0832
00:47:39.699 --> 00:47:45.179
something that we have not dared to imagine or to think.

c0833
00:47:45.179 --> 00:47:50.459
About 100 years ago, he was writing in 1850.

c0834
00:47:50.459 --> 00:47:52.340
And he's talking about 1750, you know,

c0835
00:47:52.340 --> 00:47:55.060
when the end of the Shabbatai movement,

c0836
00:47:55.060 --> 00:47:58.459
the beginning of the reform movement.

c0837
00:47:58.459 --> 00:48:03.179
The seeds of corruption were sown in these countries.

c0838
00:48:03.179 --> 00:48:08.300
In our time, they have grown like grass,

c0839
00:48:08.300 --> 00:48:12.580
taken roots, and covered the earth.

c0840
00:48:12.580 --> 00:48:15.939
They have covered the mountains of Ashkenaz.

c0841
00:48:15.939 --> 00:48:20.540
And their shadow and numerous branches have reached Italy.

c0842
00:48:20.580 --> 00:48:24.659
He knew that the life, the spiritual life of Italian Jewry,

c0843
00:48:24.659 --> 00:48:27.899
one was the gem of Judaism, of the Sephardim.

c0844
00:48:27.899 --> 00:48:31.219
All our books were printed Livorno, Mantua, Venice.

c0845
00:48:31.219 --> 00:48:33.179
All the famous, until today,

c0846
00:48:33.179 --> 00:48:34.979
when you go to the synagogue in Venice,

c0847
00:48:34.979 --> 00:48:36.899
it's just one of the most moving,

c0848
00:48:36.899 --> 00:48:38.820
moving experiences you could have,

c0849
00:48:38.820 --> 00:48:41.340
you know, or go to Florence and so on.

c0850
00:48:41.340 --> 00:48:44.300
This, he says, that was the end.

c0851
00:48:44.300 --> 00:48:50.300
He says, woe unto us, for this has taken place in our times.

c0852
00:48:50.300 --> 00:48:53.500
Who could prescribe a remedy for us?

c0853
00:48:53.500 --> 00:48:58.139
Satan is dancing among us,

c0854
00:48:58.139 --> 00:49:00.780
establishing sects in our nations,

c0855
00:49:00.780 --> 00:49:04.820
numerous parties, and different altars.

c0856
00:49:04.820 --> 00:49:11.340
This corruption of introducing novelties and dividing hearts

c0857
00:49:11.340 --> 00:49:13.739
will chase many of our beloved children

c0858
00:49:13.739 --> 00:49:16.219
away from our holy tradition.

c0859
00:49:16.219 --> 00:49:18.100
He was the first one who realized,

c0860
00:49:18.100 --> 00:49:22.659
now the Jew has the option to assimilate,

c0861
00:49:22.659 --> 00:49:26.060
and because there's so many fights among the Jews,

c0862
00:49:26.060 --> 00:49:27.860
the Jews, the intelligent Jews,

c0863
00:49:27.860 --> 00:49:32.300
they would simply choose to assimilate, to become Gorim.

c0864
00:49:32.300 --> 00:49:38.060
It will be, it will be to blame,

c0865
00:49:38.060 --> 00:49:40.860
we will be to blame if the name of Israel

c0866
00:49:40.860 --> 00:49:43.100
is never again to be mentioned here.

c0867
00:49:43.100 --> 00:49:45.739
God save us.

c0868
00:49:45.739 --> 00:49:49.939
Now, what was the idea of this Hakham?

c0869
00:49:49.939 --> 00:49:52.340
Hakham was a reasonable idea.

c0870
00:49:52.340 --> 00:49:59.820
His idea was to have a renaissance

c0871
00:49:59.820 --> 00:50:04.620
of the old Sepharadi intellectual tradition

c0872
00:50:04.620 --> 00:50:08.060
as it was prescribed by Rambam.

c0873
00:50:08.060 --> 00:50:11.500
Let me explain you in what way he was different

c0874
00:50:11.500 --> 00:50:16.500
than both the Reform and the Orthodox.

c0875
00:50:16.500 --> 00:50:20.100
The Orthodox believed that the study,

c0876
00:50:20.100 --> 00:50:25.419
any kind of secular study, it's harmful,

c0877
00:50:25.419 --> 00:50:28.699
and therefore the way to survive

c0878
00:50:28.699 --> 00:50:35.340
would be by pulling away from the culture of the Gorim

c0879
00:50:35.340 --> 00:50:39.459
and try to look only inwardly.

c0880
00:50:39.459 --> 00:50:41.580
Now, one second, we're going to know why he did,

c0881
00:50:41.580 --> 00:50:42.739
you're not going to believe it,

c0882
00:50:42.739 --> 00:50:45.580
simply you're not going to believe it.

c0883
00:50:45.580 --> 00:50:49.739
Now, because of our own Sepharadi tradition,

c0884
00:50:49.739 --> 00:50:55.100
we believe that it's possible to study

c0885
00:50:55.100 --> 00:50:57.739
the culture of the Gorim,

c0886
00:50:57.739 --> 00:51:00.179
and not only not to assimilate,

c0887
00:51:00.179 --> 00:51:04.340
but to use it to strengthen us.

c0888
00:51:04.340 --> 00:51:08.699
So he becomes, eventually becomes the chief Rabbi of Rome,

c0889
00:51:08.699 --> 00:51:14.699
and one of the things that he does is to establish schools

c0890
00:51:14.699 --> 00:51:21.899
by which a Jewish boy will be able to study Tora

c0891
00:51:21.899 --> 00:51:26.379
and at the same time participate,

c0892
00:51:26.379 --> 00:51:29.139
go to school, go to university,

c0893
00:51:29.139 --> 00:51:33.020
and be able to be part of the Gorim world.

c0894
00:51:33.020 --> 00:51:37.500
Now, here comes the most daring things.

c0895
00:51:37.500 --> 00:51:39.459
Who are the Gorim?

c0896
00:51:39.459 --> 00:51:42.300
Who are the Gorim?

c0897
00:51:42.300 --> 00:51:48.340
Of course, if you would ask the average Gentile of the time,

c0898
00:51:48.340 --> 00:51:50.060
certainly the average Jew,

c0899
00:51:50.060 --> 00:51:55.500
he'd say, well, the Gorim is the secular philosophy of the Enlightenment.

c0900
00:51:55.500 --> 00:51:57.179
What is the Enlightenment?

c0901
00:51:57.179 --> 00:51:59.459
There are people like Voltaire, let me explain about that,

c0902
00:51:59.459 --> 00:52:00.860
who believe.

c0903
00:52:00.860 --> 00:52:11.060
Religion is fanaticism,

c0904
00:52:11.060 --> 00:52:16.379
is the stage of an undeveloped mind.

c0905
00:52:16.379 --> 00:52:17.459
Yes?

c0906
00:52:17.459 --> 00:52:19.820
It belongs to the savages.

c0907
00:52:19.820 --> 00:52:20.860
All right?

c0908
00:52:20.860 --> 00:52:22.340
And among the religion,

c0909
00:52:22.340 --> 00:52:29.419
the most savage and backwards is Judaism.

c0910
00:52:29.419 --> 00:52:33.540
So therefore, if you want to be a modern person,

c0911
00:52:33.540 --> 00:52:35.780
you have to be a modern person.

c0912
00:52:35.780 --> 00:52:37.699
You have to, first of all,

c0913
00:52:37.699 --> 00:52:41.300
shed away all aspects of religion.

c0914
00:52:41.300 --> 00:52:45.379
So once that you entered into the French culture of the time,

c0915
00:52:45.379 --> 00:52:48.100
the Enlightenment,

c0916
00:52:48.100 --> 00:52:49.780
then you want to be cultured,

c0917
00:52:49.780 --> 00:52:57.020
then you cannot be possibly religious and a modern person at the same time.

c0918
00:52:57.020 --> 00:53:02.100
That was the culture that was promoted by the secularists,

c0919
00:53:02.100 --> 00:53:04.739
that was the culture of Napoleon,

c0920
00:53:04.739 --> 00:53:09.899
that was the culture of the French Empire.

c0921
00:53:09.899 --> 00:53:13.379
What Israel Moshe Hazzan was proposing is,

c0922
00:53:13.379 --> 00:53:16.620
no, there's other aspects of Gorim.

c0923
00:53:16.620 --> 00:53:20.260
There are also Gorim who are humanists.

c0924
00:53:20.260 --> 00:53:23.939
There are Gorim who cherish religion.

c0925
00:53:23.939 --> 00:53:27.820
There are Gorim who cherish literature,

c0926
00:53:27.820 --> 00:53:29.899
who cherish history.

c0927
00:53:29.899 --> 00:53:31.979
So instead of saying,

c0928
00:53:31.979 --> 00:53:37.300
all the Gorim are like those secularists,

c0929
00:53:37.300 --> 00:53:43.500
let us try to see some of the good things that the Gorim do

c0930
00:53:43.500 --> 00:53:50.580
and establish a relationship with the Gorim who appreciate us.

c0931
00:53:50.580 --> 00:53:52.340
Now, I'm going to tell you something I did.

c0932
00:53:52.340 --> 00:53:53.540
You're going to disagree.

c0933
00:53:53.540 --> 00:53:56.620
I'm not here to judge or to this.

c0934
00:53:56.620 --> 00:54:01.780
Therefore, he thought that if we Jews have a choice

c0935
00:54:01.780 --> 00:54:08.780
between becoming a citizen of Napoleon

c0936
00:54:08.780 --> 00:54:10.179
or a Roman citizen,

c0937
00:54:10.179 --> 00:54:15.020
which at the time means a citizen under the jurisdiction of whom?

c0938
00:54:15.020 --> 00:54:16.540
Of the Pope.

c0939
00:54:16.540 --> 00:54:19.020
We should choose the Pope.

c0940
00:54:19.020 --> 00:54:20.820
Why?

c0941
00:54:20.820 --> 00:54:23.100
Why?

c0942
00:54:23.100 --> 00:54:29.899
Because the Pope at least understands what religion is all about.

c0943
00:54:29.899 --> 00:54:33.899
The Pope respects religion.

c0944
00:54:33.899 --> 00:54:40.379
Yes, there is more for us to speak with the Pope

c0945
00:54:40.379 --> 00:54:43.580
than with a philosopher like Voltaire.

c0946
00:54:43.580 --> 00:54:49.060
Voltaire says, Judaism, he says, there are common roots.

c0947
00:54:49.100 --> 00:54:54.540
Now, what he did, he was the chief Rabbi of Rome.

c0948
00:54:54.540 --> 00:54:59.219
Not only that he had good relationship with the Pope,

c0949
00:54:59.219 --> 00:55:01.860
when it was the birthday of the Pope,

c0950
00:55:01.860 --> 00:55:03.860
he wrote a beautiful poetry.

c0951
00:55:03.860 --> 00:55:08.580
He wrote a poem in Hebrew, the quote of the Pope.

c0952
00:55:08.580 --> 00:55:11.020
Now, one second.

c0953
00:55:11.020 --> 00:55:14.459
You know how many, it's published, it was published.

c0954
00:55:14.780 --> 00:55:21.459
He wrote a poem in honor of the Pope.

c0955
00:55:21.459 --> 00:55:25.939
You know how many lives this poem saved?

