c1017
00:59:02.459 --> 00:59:05.219
So extraordinary that I have to read it to you

c1018
00:59:05.219 --> 00:59:09.219
because if I tell you orally, you simply will not believe it.

c1019
00:59:09.219 --> 00:59:11.260
The first thing that Rabbi Seymour Shahazan came out

c1020
00:59:11.260 --> 00:59:14.459
is with a need for us.

c1021
00:59:14.459 --> 00:59:17.899
I'm talking about 100 years before the first Zionist

c1022
00:59:17.899 --> 00:59:22.979
Congress, over 100 years before Ben Yehuda.

c1023
00:59:22.979 --> 00:59:25.979
The first thing that Rabbi Seymour Shahazan wanted

c1024
00:59:25.979 --> 00:59:32.100
was the revival of Hebrew as a spoken language.

c1025
00:59:32.100 --> 00:59:32.979
All right?

c1026
00:59:32.979 --> 00:59:36.899
Let me tell you what he has to say.

c1027
00:59:36.899 --> 00:59:38.260
It's an extraordinary thing.

c1028
00:59:38.260 --> 00:59:40.219
Extraordinary things, yes.

c1029
00:59:40.219 --> 00:59:41.580
All right.

c1030
00:59:41.580 --> 00:59:44.260
He was against becoming citizens of the country,

c1031
00:59:44.260 --> 00:59:46.620
against making revolution.

c1032
00:59:46.620 --> 00:59:48.179
If we are to make a revolution, it's

c1033
00:59:48.179 --> 00:59:52.060
going to be to take Israel now.

c1034
00:59:52.739 --> 00:59:53.239
All right.

c1035
00:59:53.239 --> 00:59:54.979
Now, let me tell you this.

c1036
00:59:54.979 --> 01:00:04.020
In 1842, 17 years before the birth of Eliezer Ben Yehuda,

c1037
01:00:04.020 --> 01:00:07.219
if you ask who is the father of the Hebrew, mother in Hebrew,

c1038
01:00:07.219 --> 01:00:08.979
Eliezer Ben Yehuda, that's not true.

c1039
01:00:08.979 --> 01:00:11.219
You know who started with all this language?

c1040
01:00:11.219 --> 01:00:14.379
Somebody who had heard Seymour Shahazan.

c1041
01:00:14.379 --> 01:00:20.100
A wonderful, wonderful person, wrote dozens of books,

c1042
01:00:20.100 --> 01:00:22.820
and was born in England.

c1043
